<title>UK: Eurobonds await France Telecom $400 mln 5-yr deal.</title>
<headline>Eurobonds await France Telecom $400 mln 5-yr deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following a busy session on Tuesday, further dollar issuance is exected today.</p>
<p>France Telecom is due to launch a $400 million five-year Eurobond via Morgan Stanley and Societe Generale, dealers said.</p>
<p>Spread talk is 15 basis points over U.S. Treasury notes.</p>
<p>Roadshows in London include a presentation by Venezuela ahead of a seven-year mark Eurobond, expected to be launched on Thursday.</p>
<p>Issue size of 900 million marks is expected at a spread of 430 to 450 b.p. over government bonds.</p>
<p>The Premier of Ontario Mike Harris will address the Canada-UK Chamber of Commerce. Ontario is said to be planning a jumbo dollar bond, possibly in the near future.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
